module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an unhandled state falls to the NOT-YET arm, so a settled answer is reported as a pending one** (a fold reduces a producer's conclusion set to a verdict with an arm per state it knows and a default for the rest, and the default it falls to is NOT-YET-TERMINAL. ",

    "A state the producer really can emit, but the fold has no arm for, is therefore rendered as STILL WAITING -- and waiting is the one disposition that never resolves, because nothing further is coming. ",

    "THE DISGUISE IS THE WHOLE DEFECT: an unhandled state normally announces itself by producing a wrong answer, and this one produces NO answer, which is indistinguishable from the fold working correctly over a subject that has not finished. ",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, gunbc PR 10086: `dashboard-ops reviews` reported ready:false with requirement `checks` failing and checks_state `pending`, AT THE SAME INSTANT that GitHub reported the head CLEAN and mergeStateStatus admitted a merge -- and the merge was then taken on GitHub's word, with no override, and was correct. ",

    "Every job in the run had a terminal conclusion: five `pass` and one `skipping`. ",

    "The skip is the unhandled state -- a GitHub NEUTRAL, which is a THIRD conclusion beside success and failure -- and the readiness fold, carrying arms for the first two, dropped it into not-yet-terminal. ",

    "THE MECHANISM IS NOT LAG AND THAT IS THE POINT: the two are the same field with the same value, and only one of them is discharged by waiting. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, and it is the load-bearing part because the status field cannot answer it: when a readiness or aggregate verdict says NOT YET, do not wait on the verdict -- NAME THE SPECIFIC ROW THAT IS NON-TERMINAL AND ASK WHETHER IT CAN EVER BECOME TERMINAL. ",

    "A row already sitting in a terminal state the fold does not recognise never will, so patience is not a remedy for it and no amount of it produces new information. ",

    "The falsifier is cheap and available at every such moment: read the producer's own per-row conclusions beside the fold's summary. ",

    "If every row is terminal and the summary is not, the summary has an arm missing. ",

    "WHY THIS LOCATION IS WORSE THAN A LOG READER, which is the reason it is ranked rather than merely filed: this is the instrument that decides whether WORK IS DONE. ",

    "A log reader that under-reports costs a diagnosis and the next reader recovers it; a readiness fold that under-reports costs the MERGE, and it fails in the direction that LOOKS LIKE CAUTION, so nobody overrides it and nobody is embarrassed by it. ",

    "THE COUNTERFACTUAL IS WHAT MAKES THE ROW ACTIONABLE: a reader following the dashboard alone would still be waiting on a pull request that had been mergeable for an hour -- and would read their own patience as diligence, which is the one failure mode that generates no complaint from the person suffering it. ",

    "WHY THIS IS NOT `empty_capture_read_as_clean_result`, its nearest neighbour and the class the same session had just extended: that class is about a CAPTURE that is empty, where the reader holds no observation and believes they hold one. ",

    "Here the observation is complete and correct at every input -- five passes and a skip, all present, all read -- and the loss is in the REDUCTION over them. ",

    "Merging the two would repeat exactly the defect that produced this row's neighbour, a recognition rule too broad to catch a second instance of its own subject: `size the artifact before grepping it` is the surviving rule there and it is silent here, because the artifact is the right size and says the right thing. ",

    "WHY THIS IS NOT `state_space_conflation`, the honest neighbour on the other side: all three of that class's forms are defects in a domain THIS TREE MODELS -- an `Option` overloaded past two meanings, a prose dichotomy over three states, a real state carried as an ad-hoc spelling -- and each of their recognition rules ends in ADD THE CONSTRUCTOR OR THE ARM. ",

    "That repair is unavailable here: the conclusion set is GitHub's and the fold is the dashboard's, neither of which this repository owns, so the actionable rule has to be one a READER can execute against an instrument they cannot edit. ",

    "That is why the rule above is a discriminator rather than a modelling instruction, and it is the whole reason this is its own row. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent wrongness for any consumer of the summary field alone, since the fold reports a value that is not merely imprecise but WRONG about whether the subject can still change, and offers no signal that an input was unrecognised. ",

    "It is mitigatable for a reader who applies the rule above, which is diligence rather than a mechanism. ",

    "CEILING: outside the modeled guarantee for the dashboard's own fold, which this repository does not own and can only observe; for the equivalent folds gunbc DOES own, structurally impossible, because a reduction over a CLOSED conclusion set is exactly the case DESIGN section 4's exhaustive match makes unwritable -- a state with no arm fails to compile rather than defaulting. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for the part we own: every gunbc fold over a third-party status or conclusion set ingesting that set as a closed coproduct in `extdeps/` with a variant per documented state, so an unmodeled state is a typed, located refusal at the boundary rather than a silent fall-through -- and NOT a default arm that maps the unknown to pending, which is this row's defect re-authored one layer down.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
